<%# The "You May Also Like" section, rendered at build time from the embedding ranking the api
    computes (data/related.json, via `rake import:related`). Renders nothing when the entry has
    no neighbors, which is what collapsed the widget this replaced.

    ⚠️ scope_entry_ids is load-bearing: read_next renders further summary cards on this same
    page, and a semantically-related entry is quite often also the chronologically adjacent one.
    Unscoped, the two cards would share a DOM id and both aria-labelledby references would
    resolve to the first. `article` is a required local. %>
<% related = related_articles(article) %>
<% if related.present? %>
  <%= partial 'partials/collection', locals: { title: "You May Also Like", items: related, variant: "halves", scope_entry_ids: true } %>
<% end %>
